Simple Task Manager

A console-based Task Manager application written in Java. Built to practice OOP, collections, file I/O, and Stream API.

Features
- Add tasks with a title and description
- View tasks in a clean, single-line format with their completion status.
- Complete or remove tasks (with automatic ID re-indexing so numbers stay sequential).
- Filter tasks to show only completed ones using Java Stream API.
- File persistence: Tasks are automatically saved to a file (`tasks.txt`) on exit and loaded back when the app starts.
- Robust input handling: Prevents app crashes if the user inputs incorrect data types.

Tech Stack
- Java 8+
- OOP & Collections (`ArrayList`)
- Stream API & Lambdas
- Java I/O (`FileWriter`, `BufferedReader`)

How to Run
1. Clone the repository or download the source code.
2. Open it in your favorite IDE (like IntelliJ IDEA or VS Code).
3. Run the `Main` class.
